#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1677
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "`Fly.io` gives no way to read its bills, so Potok estimates them itself. Every quarter of an hour it reads which machines run and how big they are, how big the database and the stored files are and how much data went out, and writes what each <CostHour>hour</CostHour> cost by the price list. The hours it missed, back to the start of the month, are filled in from `Fly.io`'s own metrics of those hours, which go back about ten days, and the rest from what runs now. Once a month is billed, one of the people who run Potok copies the sum from the <Invoice>invoice</Invoice>, and only they may. Anyone sees both on the costs page, even without an account."
