#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1585
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "When a <Value>value</Value> comes to a collection whose process has a graph, a <ValueProcess>process instance</ValueProcess> starts in the same transaction, with a copy of the graph, so changing the rule later leaves it as it was. Each element runs in a transaction of its own together with the instance's move to the next, so what it writes happens once. The instance waits on a task until someone holding the task's role picks an outcome or the deadline passes, and on a timer until it is due; a scheduler on every server takes forward those whose time has come. An action that fails leaves the instance failed where it stopped, for an editor to take up again, and removing the rule cancels the instances that run or wait. Nobody learns from a process who wrote an anonymous value."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1272
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Runs a process"
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1274
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A collection's rule can carry the graph of a process, which Potok checks as the app saves it and runs for every new <Value>value</Value>: messages, sub-groups and pushes signed by the process's own <Profile>profile</Profile>, tasks for the people of a role, deadlines and timers. The app lists the <ValueProcess>instances</ValueProcess> of the values its viewer may read, lets whoever holds a task's role finish it, and lets its editors take a failed one up again or cancel one. Each move reaches the app live. Processes the group's editors draw in Potok on the same collection stay out of the app's sight: it neither lists nor finishes their instances."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1591
