msgid "A process asks a person with a form"
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1609
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A step of a drawing may be a form: it stops the <ValueProcess>process instance</ValueProcess> until a person fills in an <GroupEntity>entity</GroupEntity> of plain attributes, each as its type, as the drawing was saved with it. It may say something first, and start with something in some attributes, worked out from what the instance holds when the form is opened; the person may change it, and what they send counts. It asks whoever started the instance, or the people of a role, and only a member of the group answers, once. The form opens by itself only for the one who started the instance, and only when it was their own step that led to it: a message they wrote, a start by hand, a form before it. Reached after a wait or someone else's decision, and for a role, it waits on the group's Processes tab. What was filled in is read by the steps that follow, an attribute at a time, with who filled it in, and whoever filled it in sets off those steps. Nobody starts a process on a schedule, so its form asks a role, and an instance nobody started fails on a form that asks whoever did. While it waits for a person, on a form or a decision, an instance keeps whom it asks, so a group's page counts what waits for its viewer without reading every waiting instance, and counts again only on news that is theirs. The same count stands on the bar's hand beside the join requests the person may approve, the Requests page lists those tasks by group, and an amber mark stands on the rows of the groups they wait in and of those above them."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1497
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <GroupMembership>membership</GroupMembership> remembers until when its member silenced the group: an hour, eight hours, a week or until they turn it on again. Until then nothing that goes to everyone reaches them as a push: new values, polls, events, an app's notices, a process's push to everyone. What is meant for them still does: a mention, an answer to their value, a reaction, a process asking them or their role. The group's unread values leave the home badge and the sums of the groups above it, while its own row still shows them, in grey. The threads of a silenced group are silent too."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1495
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A member can silence a group"
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:371
